{
  "id": "cyclic-sort-array",
  "questionId": "cyclic-sort-array",
  "slug": "cyclic-sort-array",
  "title": "Sort Array by Cyclic Placement",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Cyclic sort",
  "patterns": [
    "cyclic sort",
    "array"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "you know exactly where every value belongs in the final sorted array before you even start sorting - value v belongs at index v-1. does that change how you'd approach sorting?",
    "walk through the array with a pointer i. while nums[i] doesn't equal i+1, swap nums[i] with the element currently at index nums[i]-1 (its correct home), then check again at i",
    "once nums[i] == i+1, move on to i+1. each swap places at least one value in its final position, so the whole process finishes in linear time",
    "this is a full sort by direct placement, not a comparison sort - no comparisons between arbitrary pairs are needed at all"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "advancing the outer pointer after every swap instead of re-checking the same index until it holds its correct value",
    "using a general sort function, which works but defeats the point of practicing the O(n) placement technique",
    "off-by-one when computing the target index (value v goes to index v-1, not v)"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array `nums` of length n that contains every integer from\n1 to n exactly once, in some scrambled order.\n\n**Return the array sorted in ascending order.**\n\nSince every value already has a known \"correct\" index in the final sorted array, aim to solve this using the cyclic sort placement technique rather than a general-purpose sort.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "array length is n, and it contains a permutation of [1, n]",
      "return the array sorted in ascending order"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "array already sorted",
      "array sorted in fully reverse order",
      "array of length 1"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
